{"id":"b704bd521f4cdc1f","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-df-exponential-sums.md","title":"Exponential Sums","display":"df-exponential-sums — Exponential Sums","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-exponential-sums","aliases":["58-df-exponential-sums","Exponential Sums"],"display":"df-exponential-sums — Exponential Sums","depends_on":["[[58-df-trigonometric-sum]]","[[58-df-weyl]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-exponential-sums"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-exponential-sums</span><span>Exponential Sums</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-exponential-sums — Exponential Sums"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"1ded503967fe2f50\" href=\"?note=1ded503967fe2f50\" title=\"58-df-trigonometric-sum\">58-df-trigonometric-sum</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5056e5ab9eec996f\" href=\"?note=5056e5ab9eec996f\" title=\"58-df-weyl\">58-df-weyl</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land f\\in\\mathbb R^{\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}}\\land S\\in\\mathbb C\">\\(N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land f\\in\\mathbb R^{\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}}\\land S\\in\\mathbb C\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ExponentialSum}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{ExponentialSum}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}sums} \\vdash \\mathrm{ExponentialSum}_S(S,N,f) \\;\\leftrightarrow\\; N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land f\\in\\mathbb R^{\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}}\\land S\\in\\mathbb C\\land S=\\sum_{n=1}^N e^{2\\pi i f(n)}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}sums} \\vdash \\mathrm{ExponentialSum}_S(S,N,f) \\;\\leftrightarrow\\; N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land f\\in\\mathbb R^{\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}}\\land S\\in\\mathbb C\\land S=\\sum_{n=1}^N e^{2\\pi i f(n)}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Exponential sums: finite sums of exponential phases; count oscillatory behavior</li>\n<li>Weyl sum: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sum e^{2\\pi i P(n)/q}\">\\(\\sum e^{2\\pi i P(n)/q}\\)</span>; character sums over finite fields</li>\n<li>Vinogradov: Weyl bounds; used in Waring's problem and circle method</li>\n<li>Roughness: bounding <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|S|\">\\(|S|\\)</span> from above controls additive energy; applications in number theory</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Vaughan, The Hardy-Littlewood Method</li>\n<li>Iwaniec, Spectral Methods of Automorphic Forms</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-trigonometric-sum","status":"resolved","id":"1ded503967fe2f50","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-trigonometric-sum]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-weyl","status":"resolved","id":"5056e5ab9eec996f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-weyl]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land f\\in\\mathbb R^{\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}}\\land S\\in\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ExponentialSum}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}exponential\\text{-}sums} \\vdash \\mathrm{ExponentialSum}_S(S,N,f) \\;\\leftrightarrow\\; N\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land f\\in\\mathbb R^{\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}}\\land S\\in\\mathbb C\\land S=\\sum_{n=1}^N e^{2\\pi i f(n)}","display":true},{"tex":"\\sum e^{2\\pi i P(n)/q}","display":false},{"tex":"|S|","display":false}],"bytes":1156,"backlinks":[{"id":"04cbb7a8958985d0","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$S_N(f)=\\sum_{n=1}^N e^{2\\pi i f(n)}$ (exponential sum, see [[58-df-exponential-sums]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-505","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-exponential-sums.md|58-df-exponential-sums]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["1ded503967fe2f50","5056e5ab9eec996f"]}